# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES Phase 3 unit 3.11 — THE TERMINAL DELETE IS NOT RECORDED
# `Samen.Scopes.Docs.PagePurge` writes `record_purged` in the destroy's own transaction, so the trail
# names the irreversible delete the way it named the archive that preceded it. This patch drops that
# write: the page still disappears and the guard still holds — a SILENT destroy, which is exactly the
# state a "who removed this?" question must never be able to reach.
#
# Aimed at the AUDIT CALL only. The archive-first refusal, the action body, the policy and the
# cascade are untouched.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_trash_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: an admin empties a page
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/page_purge.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/page_purge.ex
@@ -39,8 +39,7 @@
   def change(changeset, _opts, _context) do
     case archived_state(changeset) do
       :archived ->
-        Ash.Changeset.after_action(changeset, fn cs, record ->
-          Samen.Archival.Audit.write(cs, record, "record_purged")
+        Ash.Changeset.after_action(changeset, fn _cs, record ->
           {:ok, record}
         end)
 
